1
00:01:58,150 --> 00:02:01,150
You did this. You did this!

2
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:04,110
-We have to leave.  -Take him! Take him!

3
00:02:07,010 --> 00:02:08,360
Where is his wife?

4
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:10,540
Where's Sansa?

5
00:02:10,550 --> 00:02:13,040
Find her. Bar the gates of the city.

6
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:14,770
Seize every ship in the harbor.

7
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:19,150
-Where is she?!  -No one leaves the capital!

8
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:20,490
No one!

9
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:51,460
-Get in.  -Where are we going?

10
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:52,810
Somewhere safe.

11
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,160
Up you go, my lady.

12
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:44,550
You'll be fine.

13
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:46,300
You're stronger than you know.

14
00:04:05,570 --> 00:04:07,540
-Lord Baelish?  -Petyr.

15
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:09,920
Are you hurt, my lady?

16
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,840
Good. Good.

17
00:04:11,990 --> 00:04:14,350
I'm sure you've had quite a fright. Rest easy.

18
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:16,380
-The worst is past.  -Lord Baelish.

19
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,770
I promised I'd get her to you safely.

20
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:19,360
Softly, my friend.

21
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,760
Voices carry over water.

22
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:24,800
I should get back before someone thinks to look for me.

23
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,470
First you'll want your pay.

24
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:29,440
-10,000, was it?  -10,000.

25
00:04:35,490 --> 00:04:36,410
Wait!

26
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,880
You don't want the queen to hear, do you?

27
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,360
1,000 gold cloaks are searching for you.

28
00:04:45,730 --> 00:04:47,190
And if they found you,

29
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:51,130
how do you think they would punish the girl who murdered the king?

30
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:54,490
-I didn't murder anyone.  -I know. I know.

31
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,780
But you must admit it looks suspicious.

32
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:58,000
The king who executed your father,

33
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,050
who tormented you for years,

34
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:02,460
and you fled the scene of his murder.

35
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:05,160
Why did you kill him?

36
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,670
Because he was a drunk and a fool,

37
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,210
and I don't trust drunk fools.

38
00:05:11,430 --> 00:05:12,770
He saved me.

39
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:15,830
Saved you? My lady, he followed my orders.

40
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:19,560
Every one of them. And he did it all for gold.

41
00:05:20,310 --> 00:05:23,030
Money buys a man's silence for a time.

42
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:26,000
A bolt in the heart buys it forever.

43
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:31,480
He was helping me because I saved his life.

44
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:35,680
Yes, and he gave you a priceless necklace

45
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:38,530
that once belonged to his grandmother.

46
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:41,650
The last legacy of House Hollard.

47
00:05:50,310 --> 00:05:52,390
I had it made a few weeks ago.

48
00:05:53,970 --> 00:05:56,430
What did I once tell you about the capital?

49
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,240
We're all liars here.

50
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:03,290
Come, my lady.

51
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:05,320
I know you've had a difficult day.

52
00:06:06,330 --> 00:06:07,740
But you're safe now.

53
00:06:08,390 --> 00:06:10,090
I promise you that.

54
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:12,590
You're safe with me

55
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,910
and sailing home.

56
00:06:21,490 --> 00:06:23,130
So am I the queen?

57
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,820
More than you were with Renly.

58
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:29,150
Less than you would have been if Joffrey had done you the courtesy

59
00:06:29,150 --> 00:06:32,130
of consummating the marriage before dying.

60
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:36,660
In any case, this would not be an opportune moment to press the issue.

61
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:38,930
Clawing at his own throat,

62
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:41,820
looking to his mother to make it stop, it was horrible.

63
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:44,130
The world is overflowing with horrible things.

64
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:46,440
But they're all a tray of cakes next to death.

65
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,180
They brought me your grandfather's body when he died, you know?

66
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,970
Made me look at it.

67
00:06:53,310 --> 00:06:54,490
What was it like?

68
00:06:54,550 --> 00:06:57,960
They took me to the Great Hall and there he was.

69
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,000
The man I'd married

70
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,220
and suffered to father my children.

71
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:05,440
A great doughy lump I'd sat next to

72
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:08,870
at endless dinners and tedious gatherings.

73
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:11,250
There he was,

74
00:07:12,050 --> 00:07:13,680
lying on a table.

75
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:20,010
One of my husbands preferred the company of men

76
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:21,930
and was stabbed through the heart.

77
00:07:21,930 --> 00:07:24,250
Another was happiest torturing animals

78
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:26,410
and was poisoned at our wedding feast.

79
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:28,650
-I must be cursed.  -Nonsense.

80
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:31,750
Your circumstances have improved markedly.

81
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:35,760
You may not have enjoyed watching him die,

82
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:37,940
but you enjoyed it more than you would have enjoyed

83
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:40,250
being married to him, I can promise you that.

84
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:42,070
But I would have been the queen.

85
00:07:42,070 --> 00:07:43,620
Our alliance with the Lannisters

86
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:46,560
remains every bit as necessary to them

87
00:07:46,570 --> 00:07:48,800
as it is unpleasant for us.

88
00:07:49,610 --> 00:07:51,690
You did wonderful work on Joffrey.

89
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,290
The next one should be easier.

90
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:06,820
Your brother is dead.

91
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:10,180
Do you know what that means?

92
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,720
I'm not trying to trick you.

93
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,020
It means I'll become king.

94
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,320
Yes, you will become king.

95
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:25,490
What kind of king do you think you'll be?

96
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,510
A good king?

97
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:30,890
Mm, I think so as well.

98
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:34,800
You've got the right temperament for it.

99
00:08:36,570 --> 00:08:39,460
But what makes a good king?

100
00:08:39,770 --> 00:08:42,940
What is a good king's single most important quality?

101
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:45,050
This is hardly the place or the time.

102
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,420
Holiness?

103
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:52,560
Baelor the Blessed was holy.

104
00:08:52,850 --> 00:08:54,200
And pious.

105
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:56,250
He built this sept.

106
00:08:57,500 --> 00:09:00,620
He also named a six-year-old boy high septon,

107
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:03,640
because he thought the boy could work miracles.

108
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:08,040
He ended up fasting himself into an early grave,

109
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:10,010
because food was of this world

110
00:09:10,010 --> 00:09:12,100
and this world was sinful.

111
00:09:15,210 --> 00:09:16,460
Justice.

112
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:17,720
Yeah.

113
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:20,330
A good king must be just.

114
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,520
Orys I was just.

115
00:09:24,350 --> 00:09:26,670
Everyone applauded his reforms.

116
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:28,980
Nobles and commoners alike.

117
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:30,840
But he wasn't just for long.

118
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:35,960
He was murdered in his sleep after less than a year by his own brother.

119
00:09:36,830 --> 00:09:38,750
Was that truly just of him?

120
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:40,930
To abandon his subjects to an evil

121
00:09:40,930 --> 00:09:43,540
that he was too gullible to recognize?

122
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:45,440
-No.  -No.

123
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:50,620
-What about strength?  -Yes.

124
00:09:50,650 --> 00:09:52,090
Strength.

125
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:55,090
King Robert was strong.

126
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,570
He won the rebellion

127
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,510
and crushed the Targaryen dynasty.

128
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:06,570
And he attended three small council meetings in 17 years.

129
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:10,240
He spent his time whoring and hunting and drinking,

130
00:10:10,870 --> 00:10:12,890
until the last two killed him.

131
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:17,990
So, we have a man who starves himself to death,

132
00:10:18,230 --> 00:10:20,700
a man who lets his own brother murder him,

133
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:24,970
and a man who thinks that winning and ruling are the same thing.

134
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:29,790
What do they all lack?

135
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:36,710
-Wisdom.  -Yes!

136
00:10:36,710 --> 00:10:38,350
Wisdom is what makes a good king.

137
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,560
Yes.

138
00:10:40,570 --> 00:10:42,670
But what is wisdom?

139
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:47,960
A house with great wealth and fertile lands

140
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,700
asks you for your protection

141
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:52,690
against another house with a strong navy

142
00:10:52,710 --> 00:10:54,570
that could one day oppose you.

143
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:58,610
How do you know which choice is wise and which isn't?

144
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:02,150
You've any experience of treasuries and granaries

145
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:04,200
or shipyards and soldiers?

146
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:07,300
-No.  -No. Of course not.

147
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:11,150
A wise king knows what he knows and what he doesn't.

148
00:11:11,910 --> 00:11:13,330
You're young.

149
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:16,320
A wise young king listens to his counselors

150
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:19,350
and heeds their advice until he comes of age.

151
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,740
And the wisest kings

152
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:25,130
continue to listen to them long afterwards.

153
00:11:26,910 --> 00:11:28,980
Your brother was not a wise king.

154
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:30,870
Your brother was not a good king.

155
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:32,510
If he had been,

156
00:11:33,310 --> 00:11:35,450
perhaps he'd still be alive.

157
00:11:35,850 --> 00:11:39,260
Now, as the king, you will have to marry.

158
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:41,490
Do you understand why?

159
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:43,110
A king needs a queen.

160
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,770
Yes, but why?

161
00:11:46,070 --> 00:11:48,150
To further the family line.

162
00:11:49,070 --> 00:11:51,680
-Do you know how that happens?  -Yes.

163
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:55,540
Yes, but has anyone explained the details to you?

164
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:57,480
I don't think so.

165
00:11:57,490 --> 00:11:59,680
It's all relatively straightforward.

166
00:12:00,850 --> 00:12:03,300
-How are you?  -I'm all right.

167
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,580
You are. You will be.

168
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:07,170
I'll see to that.

169
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:15,190
Please give the queen a moment alone with her son.

170
00:12:15,190 --> 00:12:17,140
-Yes, my lord.  -All of you.

171
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:48,030
It was Tyrion.

172
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:51,300
He killed him.

173
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:55,050
He told me he would.

174
00:12:56,780 --> 00:13:00,020
"A day will come when you think you are safe and happy

175
00:13:01,020 --> 00:13:04,230
and your joy will turn to ashes in your mouth."

176
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,790
That's what he said to me.

177
00:13:12,870 --> 00:13:14,340
You saw it.

178
00:13:15,550 --> 00:13:17,900
You saw Joff point at him just before he.

179
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,630
I don't know what I saw.

180
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:23,780
Avenge him.

181
00:13:25,590 --> 00:13:27,140
Avenge our son.

182
00:13:29,490 --> 00:13:30,800
Kill Tyrion.

183
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:35,420
Tyrion's my brother.

184
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:36,870
Our brother.

185
00:13:37,530 --> 00:13:40,140
There'll be a trial. We'll get to the truth of what happened.

186
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:41,750
I don't want a trial.

187
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:45,610
He'll squirm his way to freedom given the chance.

188
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:47,560
I want him dead.

189
00:13:50,750 --> 00:13:52,360
Please, Jaime.

190
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,820
You have to.

191
00:13:56,380 --> 00:13:58,040
He was our son.

192
00:13:58,830 --> 00:14:00,410
Our baby boy.

193
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:42,120
You're a hateful woman.

194
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:46,100
Why have the gods made me love a hateful woman?

195
00:14:53,830 --> 00:14:55,650
Jaime, not here, please.

196
00:14:56,310 --> 00:14:57,120
Please.

197
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,540
Stop it.

198
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:01,560
-Stop it. Stop.  -No.

199
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:05,160
Stop it. Stop.

200
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,660
Stop.

201
00:15:19,070 --> 00:15:20,670
Stop. It's not right.

202
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:25,150
It's not right. It's not right.

203
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:26,030
I don't care.

204
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:28,880
-Don't.  -I don't care.

205
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:31,160
-Don't. Jaime, don't.  -I don't care.

206
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:34,980
Gonna rain soon.

207
00:15:38,210 --> 00:15:39,340
Where are we?

208
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:44,820
Near Fairmarket, I think.

209
00:15:45,510 --> 00:15:46,470
You think?

210
00:15:46,650 --> 00:15:47,770
You don't have a map?

211
00:15:48,070 --> 00:15:51,300
-No, I don't have a map.  -Maybe we should get one.

212
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:54,390
Just point out the next map shop you see and I'll buy you one.

213
00:15:54,390 --> 00:15:55,940
How far is it to the Eyrie?

214
00:15:56,170 --> 00:15:59,220
-Far.  -And you're sure we're going the right way?

215
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:02,330
Believe me, girl, I want you there as soon as I can.

216
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:05,070
Get my gold, be on my way.

217
00:16:05,070 --> 00:16:07,960
-On your way where?  -Why do you care?

218
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:17,250
Might book passage across the Narrow Sea.

219
00:16:17,790 --> 00:16:19,320
Fight as a sellsword.

220
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:24,200
Second Sons, could be. Seems like a good fit for me.

221
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:26,280
I'd like to see Braavos one day.

222
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,550
Why Braavos?

223
00:16:29,270 --> 00:16:30,500
I have friends there.

224
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:32,750
I doubt it.

225
00:16:32,910 --> 00:16:34,510
Seven blessings to you.

226
00:16:37,450 --> 00:16:40,730
-What do you want?  -What do I want? This is my land.

227
00:16:40,730 --> 00:16:42,800
If I'm standing on it, it's my land.

228
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:45,950
We were just watering the horses. We'll be on our way.

229
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,220
Forgive my father.

230
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:54,100
He was wounded fighting in the war.

231
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:57,900
Our cottage burned down, while he was gone and my mother with it.

232
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,050
He's never been the same.

233
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,300
Which house did he fight for?

234
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:17,350
The Tullys of Riverrun.

235
00:17:21,490 --> 00:17:22,910
There's a storm coming.

236
00:17:22,910 --> 00:17:24,480
You'll be wanting a roof tonight.

237
00:17:24,910 --> 00:17:26,440
There's fresh hay in the barn.

238
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:30,220
And Sally here makes rabbit stew just like her mom used to do.

239
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:33,910
We don't have much, but any man that bled

240
00:17:33,910 --> 00:17:35,840
for House Tully is welcome to it.

241
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:43,910
We ask the Father to judge us with mercy

242
00:17:43,910 --> 00:17:45,920
accepting our human frailty.

243
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:48,220
We ask the Mother to bless our crops,

244
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:51,410
so we may feed ourselves and all who come to our door.

245
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:53,480
We ask the Warrior to give us courage

246
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,590
in these days of strife and turmoil.

247
00:17:55,590 --> 00:17:57,950
We ask the Maiden to protect Sally's virtue

248
00:17:57,950 --> 00:17:59,880
to keep her from the clutches of depravity.

249
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,000
You got to do all seven of the fuckers?

250
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,020
Father!

251
00:18:07,530 --> 00:18:10,380
We ask the Smith to strengthen our hands and our backs,

252
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,860
so we may finish the work required of us.

253
00:18:12,870 --> 00:18:14,390
We ask the Crone to guide us

254
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:17,060
on our journey from darkness to darkness.

255
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,980
And we ask the Stranger not to kill us

256
00:18:18,990 --> 00:18:21,310
in our beds tonight for no damn reason at all.

257
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:28,010
I'm so sorry.

258
00:18:48,830 --> 00:18:49,810
Really good.

259
00:18:50,210 --> 00:18:52,750
-Did you fight at the Twins?  -Call that a fight?

260
00:18:52,910 --> 00:18:54,850
Slaughtering livestock more like.

261
00:18:54,860 --> 00:18:56,590
The Red Wedding they're calling it.

262
00:18:57,960 --> 00:19:00,270
Walder Frey committed sacrilege that day.

263
00:19:00,270 --> 00:19:02,280
He shared bread and salt with the Starks.

264
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,460
He offered them guest right.

265
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:05,520
Guest right don't mean much anymore.

266
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,050
It means something to me.

267
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:10,740
The gods will have their vengeance.

268
00:19:11,590 --> 00:19:14,060
Frey will burn in the seventh hell for what he did.

269
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:17,580
Things were different when Hoster Tully ruled the Riverlands.

270
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:20,070
We had good years and bad years, same as anyone.

271
00:19:20,070 --> 00:19:22,810
But we were safe. Now with the Freys,

272
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:26,880
raiders come plundering, steal our food, steal our silver.

273
00:19:26,990 --> 00:19:29,140
I was gonna send Sally north to stay with my brother,

274
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:32,410
but the north's no better. The whole country's gone sour.

275
00:19:33,150 --> 00:19:34,470
You got any ale?

276
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:36,800
Afraid not.

277
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:43,250
How can a man not keep ale in his home?

278
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:47,420
You look like you could really swing that sword.

279
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,970
A real warrior with proper training.

280
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:54,240
Those raiders wouldn't stand a chance against you.

281
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:57,450
How would it be if you stayed on till the new moon?

282
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:59,760
I could use a man to help with the farmwork.

283
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:01,280
Sally does what she can,

284
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:04,060
but she can't lift a bale of hay.

285
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:06,700
And if any thieves came looking for easy pickings,

286
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:09,040
one look at you, I'd bet they'd run the other way.

287
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:13,050
Meaning no offense.

288
00:20:19,810 --> 00:20:21,080
What'll you pay?

289
00:20:21,950 --> 00:20:23,410
I don't have much.

290
00:20:24,370 --> 00:20:26,910
But I have hidden a bit of silver from the bandits.

291
00:20:29,410 --> 00:20:31,120
Fair wages for fair work?

292
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,870
Fair wages for fair work.

293
00:21:12,030 --> 00:21:14,370
-What did you do?!  -Get your horse saddled.

294
00:21:14,370 --> 00:21:17,510
-You told me you weren't a thief.  -I wasn't.

295
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:20,000
He took us in. He fed us and you.

296
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,870
Aye, he took us in. He's a good man

297
00:21:21,870 --> 00:21:23,620
and his daughter makes a nice stew.

298
00:21:23,710 --> 00:21:25,460
And they'll both be dead come winter.

299
00:21:25,650 --> 00:21:27,880
-You don't know that.  -I do know it.

300
00:21:27,950 --> 00:21:30,910
He's weak. He can't protect himself.

301
00:21:31,310 --> 00:21:33,100
They'll both be dead come winter.

302
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:35,250
Dead men don't need silver.

303
00:21:35,830 --> 00:21:39,330
You're the worst shit in the Seven Kingdoms.

304
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,140
There's plenty worse than me.

305
00:21:42,790 --> 00:21:44,770
I just understand the way things are.

306
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:48,600
How many Starks they got to behead before you figure it out?

307
00:21:52,790 --> 00:21:55,390
Raper. Raper.

308
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:57,250
Horse thief.

309
00:21:57,470 --> 00:21:58,990
Ninth born son.

310
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:00,950
Raper.

311
00:22:01,390 --> 00:22:04,030
Thief. Thief and raper.

312
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:07,220
There he is, Sam the Slayer.

313
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:09,440
Going to visit your wildling whore?

314
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:11,330
-She's not a whore.  -No?

315
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:13,690
Maybe I'll give her a copper tonight and find out.

316
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:21,000
They all think I'm lying.

317
00:22:21,610 --> 00:22:22,640
About what?

318
00:22:23,450 --> 00:22:24,990
Killing the white walker.

319
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:26,800
You're not lying.

320
00:22:27,910 --> 00:22:30,090
I'll never forget the way it screamed.

321
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:34,080
But you're the only one that saw it.

322
00:22:34,190 --> 00:22:35,750
And they all think you're just a.

323
00:22:35,950 --> 00:22:36,840
A what?

324
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:39,830
Well, a wildling.

325
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:43,360
My father hated that word.

326
00:22:43,540 --> 00:22:46,440
It's not a very nice word, I suppose.

327
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:47,570
I don't know.

328
00:22:48,710 --> 00:22:51,910
It makes me sound a bit dangerous, doesn't it?

329
00:23:04,260 --> 00:23:05,550
So,

330
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:07,660
are you all right?

331
00:23:07,670 --> 00:23:09,470
No one bothering you?

332
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:12,030
I get a lot of looks.

333
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:13,800
I hear them making their jokes.

334
00:23:13,810 --> 00:23:16,560
But no one's touched me if that's what you mean.

335
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:20,100
I worry about it sometimes.

336
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:21,950
All the time.

337
00:23:23,140 --> 00:23:24,950
Why do you worry about it?

338
00:23:25,390 --> 00:23:28,590
100 men, one woman.

339
00:23:28,830 --> 00:23:31,220
They've got other things to think about.

340
00:23:31,310 --> 00:23:33,450
That's the only thing they think about.

341
00:23:33,460 --> 00:23:36,260
-You're being silly.  -I'm not being silly.

342
00:23:36,810 --> 00:23:39,860
There's 100 men lying awake at night picturing you.

343
00:23:42,010 --> 00:23:43,250
What about you?

344
00:23:46,250 --> 00:23:47,370
What about me?

345
00:23:50,650 --> 00:23:51,500
Gilly?

346
00:23:57,590 --> 00:23:58,830
I worry about you.

347
00:24:04,330 --> 00:24:05,340
Thank you.

348
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:07,550
For what?

349
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:09,470
For worrying about me.

350
00:24:13,650 --> 00:24:16,910
I don't know if you're safe here.

351
00:24:17,820 --> 00:24:18,690
They're my brothers,

352
00:24:18,690 --> 00:24:21,510
but some of them were thieves before they came here.

353
00:24:21,510 --> 00:24:23,310
Some of them were rapers.

354
00:24:23,570 --> 00:24:25,870
You saw what they did at your father's keep.

355
00:24:27,220 --> 00:24:29,280
So what are you saying?

356
00:24:31,940 --> 00:24:36,710
Maybe you'd be safer in Mole's Town.

357
00:24:41,370 --> 00:24:43,500
Are you bored of me?

358
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:45,910
Bored of you?

359
00:24:52,380 --> 00:24:54,210
I want to protect you.

360
00:25:00,810 --> 00:25:02,700
I'll get these to Hobb.

361
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:04,570
Keep an eye on little Sam.

362
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:35,870
Your Grace.

363
00:25:37,090 --> 00:25:39,620
You're a literary man now. What do you make of that?

364
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:54,050
-Joffrey?  -The usurper Joffrey Baratheon.

365
00:25:54,080 --> 00:25:57,170
I said those words when I tossed a leech into the fire.

366
00:25:57,170 --> 00:25:59,670
A leech filled with bastard blood.

367
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:01,960
A bastard you set free.

368
00:26:02,350 --> 00:26:04,750
I am now faced with a great opportunity

369
00:26:04,750 --> 00:26:06,750
and I am powerless to take advantage of it.

370
00:26:06,750 --> 00:26:07,880
I will find you an army, Your Grace.

371
00:26:07,890 --> 00:26:08,960
I've been working day and night.

372
00:26:08,970 --> 00:26:10,470
What progress have you made?

373
00:26:11,250 --> 00:26:13,010
I've rallied House Peasebury to your cause.

374
00:26:13,010 --> 00:26:14,280
House Peasebury.

375
00:26:15,380 --> 00:26:17,890
-House Musgood.  -House Musgood.

376
00:26:17,900 --> 00:26:20,250
-And House Haigh.  -House Haigh.

377
00:26:25,310 --> 00:26:28,160
They don't have enough men between them to raid a pantry.

378
00:26:29,970 --> 00:26:31,860
Westeros is not the world, Your Grace.

379
00:26:31,860 --> 00:26:33,870
We need to look east for ships and men.

380
00:26:33,870 --> 00:26:37,150
10,000 skilled soldiers fight for the Golden Company.

381
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:39,240
-The Golden Company?  -They've never broken a contract.

382
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,330
They're sellswords.

383
00:26:40,330 --> 00:26:42,130
We're willing to use blood magic to put you on the throne,

384
00:26:42,130 --> 00:26:44,010
but we're not willing to pay men to fight?

385
00:26:44,070 --> 00:26:46,310
Now the Red Woman's magic is real.

386
00:26:46,310 --> 00:26:48,910
Her visions and prophecies may be, too,

387
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:51,700
but I've never heard of visions and prophecies winning a war.

388
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:54,070
Soldiers win wars. Soldiers on the ground.

389
00:26:54,070 --> 00:26:55,550
It's dirty on the ground.

390
00:26:55,550 --> 00:26:56,880
We don't have any gold.

391
00:26:57,430 --> 00:26:58,340
Not yet.

392
00:27:02,930 --> 00:27:04,790
If I do not press my claim,

393
00:27:04,930 --> 00:27:06,630
my claim will be forgotten.

394
00:27:06,630 --> 00:27:09,830
I will not become a page in someone else's history book.

395
00:27:11,580 --> 00:27:13,700
I'm running out of time, Ser Davos.

396
00:27:14,610 --> 00:27:16,500
Which means you're running out of time.

397
00:27:22,270 --> 00:27:23,390
You're late.

398
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:24,860
I'm sorry, Princess.

399
00:27:24,980 --> 00:27:26,360
I thought you weren't coming.

400
00:27:26,500 --> 00:27:29,350
The Hand of the King doesn't have much leisure time.

401
00:27:29,350 --> 00:27:30,500
You won't be a very good Hand

402
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:32,550
if you see the word knight and say "Ka-nigit."

403
00:27:32,550 --> 00:27:34,280
That happened once, weeks ago.

404
00:27:34,660 --> 00:27:36,500
You're your father's daughter, no mistake.

405
00:27:36,500 --> 00:27:38,560
Bloody relentless, the both of you.

406
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:41,190
It's a new one today. Lots of tricky words.

407
00:27:41,310 --> 00:27:42,790
But I think you can manage.

408
00:27:45,520 --> 00:27:47,410
You'll never read well if you move your lips.

409
00:27:47,410 --> 00:27:48,890
That's how children do it.

410
00:27:54,990 --> 00:27:59,180
"The Life and Adventures of Elyo Grivas

411
00:27:59,180 --> 00:28:01,370
First Sword of Braavos."

412
00:28:01,980 --> 00:28:03,350
Thank you very much.

413
00:28:03,910 --> 00:28:06,750
I like this one. It's full of sword fights and pirates.

414
00:28:07,340 --> 00:28:08,580
You were a pirate once.

415
00:28:08,580 --> 00:28:10,920
No, I was never a pirate. I was a smuggler.

416
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:12,250
What's the difference?

417
00:28:12,250 --> 00:28:13,690
Well, if you're a famous smuggler,

418
00:28:13,700 --> 00:28:15,170
you're not doing it right.

419
00:28:15,230 --> 00:28:16,960
My father says a criminal is a criminal.

420
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:18,700
Your father lacks an appreciation

421
00:28:18,700 --> 00:28:21,150
of the finer points of bad behavior.

422
00:28:22,380 --> 00:28:23,470
So do the Braavosi.

423
00:28:23,470 --> 00:28:25,260
-You've sailed to Braavos?  -Of course.

424
00:28:25,260 --> 00:28:27,650
Almost got beheaded by a First Sword of Braavos.

425
00:28:28,500 --> 00:28:29,590
I tried to explain to him

426
00:28:29,590 --> 00:28:32,560
the difference between pirates and smugglers,

427
00:28:32,560 --> 00:28:33,300
but he didn't seem any more

428
00:28:33,300 --> 00:28:35,890
interested in the distinction than your father.

429
00:28:36,100 --> 00:28:38,290
I suppose if you work for the Iron Bank of Braavos

430
00:28:38,290 --> 00:28:41,010
and each one of your gold barges is worth half a kingdom,

431
00:28:41,010 --> 00:28:44,530
you tend not to be overly concerned with the kind of distinction.

432
00:29:03,130 --> 00:29:05,250
-What was that for?  -I need you to write a message.

433
00:29:05,250 --> 00:29:07,500
You should write it yourself. It's good practice.

434
00:29:07,500 --> 00:29:09,050
It's too important for me.

435
00:29:09,300 --> 00:29:12,290
I need a smart person to do it. Go on.

436
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:16,340
To the offices of the Iron Bank of Braavos

437
00:29:16,660 --> 00:29:19,910
from Stannis Baratheon the one true king of Westeros.

438
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:21,680
But that's not you.

439
00:29:21,770 --> 00:29:23,260
I need to get their attention.

440
00:29:23,410 --> 00:29:25,810
Go on. Write.

441
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:37,770
He's seen some adventures, hasn't he?

442
00:29:57,960 --> 00:30:00,500
-Precious little thing.  -Thank you.

443
00:30:01,460 --> 00:30:03,790
-What's his name?  -Sam.

444
00:30:03,910 --> 00:30:05,020
Lovely.

445
00:30:06,750 --> 00:30:07,870
That the daddy?

446
00:30:07,870 --> 00:30:08,840
No.

447
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:10,020
Where's the daddy?

448
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:12,560
He's dead.

449
00:30:13,730 --> 00:30:15,430
Where you from?

450
00:30:18,240 --> 00:30:19,610
North of here.

451
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:21,240
North of here?

452
00:30:25,370 --> 00:30:26,860
You a fucking wildling?

453
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:30,670
-Only room and board?  -That's right.

454
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:33,170
She'll clean and cook

455
00:30:33,180 --> 00:30:35,090
and look after the other girls' babies.

456
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:37,940
Could find other work for her, too.

457
00:30:38,230 --> 00:30:40,400
-No other work.  -There'd be money.

458
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:41,890
Give you a piece of it.

459
00:30:42,020 --> 00:30:44,030
No other work.

460
00:31:06,090 --> 00:31:08,360
I promise to come back and visit whenever I can.

461
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:13,760
You'll be safer here.

462
00:31:14,420 --> 00:31:16,720
Who's gonna protect you at Castle Black? Me?

463
00:31:17,940 --> 00:31:19,990
You protected me north of the Wall.

464
00:31:19,990 --> 00:31:21,340
This is different.

465
00:31:21,710 --> 00:31:22,910
They're brothers of the Night's Watch,

466
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:25,050
and I can't just stab them in the back,

467
00:31:25,110 --> 00:31:27,840
and I can't run away, which is what we did at Craster's.

468
00:31:30,390 --> 00:31:32,030
You have to trust me.

469
00:31:32,940 --> 00:31:34,350
It's for the best.

470
00:31:39,810 --> 00:31:41,190
Best for you.

471
00:31:41,710 --> 00:31:43,160
Oh, Gilly.

472
00:31:45,700 --> 00:31:47,030
Please don't.

473
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:21,370
Greedy.

474
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:29,830
No?

475
00:32:30,590 --> 00:32:32,090
I'm sorry. You're lovely,

476
00:32:32,090 --> 00:32:34,140
I just never acquired the taste.

477
00:32:34,140 --> 00:32:36,910
You're calling my beauty an acquired taste?

478
00:32:37,100 --> 00:32:40,720
That's quite all right, lover. It's more for you.

479
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:44,860
Your loss.

480
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:52,500
You like them both the same?

481
00:32:53,660 --> 00:32:55,870
-Boys and girls?  -Does that surprise you?

482
00:32:55,870 --> 00:32:57,400
Everyone has a preference.

483
00:32:57,400 --> 00:32:59,810
Then everyone is missing half the world's pleasure.

484
00:33:01,540 --> 00:33:04,790
The gods made that and it delights me.

485
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:06,210
The gods made this

486
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:09,330
and it delights me.

487
00:33:09,860 --> 00:33:11,880
When it comes to war, I fight for Dorne.

488
00:33:11,880 --> 00:33:15,650
When it comes to love, I don't choose sides.

489
00:33:15,650 --> 00:33:17,990
I hope I have as much stamina when I'm your age.

490
00:33:17,990 --> 00:33:19,930
What are you, 25?

491
00:33:20,260 --> 00:33:21,550
Children.

492
00:33:23,250 --> 00:33:25,420
Someday, if you're lucky,

493
00:33:25,420 --> 00:33:27,710
you will wake up and realize you are old.

494
00:33:27,710 --> 00:33:29,450
That pretty ass of yours will sag.

495
00:33:29,450 --> 00:33:32,720
Your belly will grow soft and your back will ache in the night

496
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:36,910
and gray hairs will sprout from your ears.

497
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:39,040
No one will want you anymore.

498
00:33:39,490 --> 00:33:42,950
Make sure you fucked your fill before that day.

499
00:33:43,930 --> 00:33:45,100
Did you?

500
00:33:46,270 --> 00:33:48,490
He is a prince of Dorne.

501
00:33:49,270 --> 00:33:51,540
Girls and boys will line up

502
00:33:51,540 --> 00:33:54,720
to fuck him till the day he dies.

503
00:33:57,300 --> 00:34:00,130
They will all have to line up behind you.

504
00:34:06,070 --> 00:34:08,230
-Prince Oberyn.  -Lord Tywin.

505
00:34:08,520 --> 00:34:10,120
May we have the room?

506
00:34:14,300 --> 00:34:16,040
Call my name if you need me, lover.

507
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:28,930
Would you like to sit?

508
00:34:29,480 --> 00:34:30,680
No, thank you.

509
00:34:31,370 --> 00:34:32,620
Some wine?

510
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:34,510
No, thank you.

511
00:34:36,560 --> 00:34:39,070
-I'm sorry about your grandson.  -Are you?

512
00:34:39,820 --> 00:34:43,650
I don't believe that a child is responsible for the sins of his father.

513
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:46,120
Or his grandfather.

514
00:34:47,030 --> 00:34:48,670
An awful way to die.

515
00:34:49,430 --> 00:34:50,830
Which way is that?

516
00:34:51,330 --> 00:34:53,600
Are you interrogating me, Lord Tywin?

517
00:34:53,680 --> 00:34:55,780
Some believe the king choked.

518
00:34:55,900 --> 00:34:57,950
Some believe the sky is blue, because we live

519
00:34:57,950 --> 00:35:00,290
inside the eye of a blue-eyed giant.

520
00:35:02,710 --> 00:35:04,410
The king was poisoned.

521
00:35:05,230 --> 00:35:07,890
I hear you studied poisons at the Citadel.

522
00:35:07,890 --> 00:35:10,190
I did. This is why I know.

523
00:35:10,190 --> 00:35:13,780
Your hatred for my family is rather well known.

524
00:35:14,020 --> 00:35:16,700
You arrive at the capital, an expert in poisoning,

525
00:35:16,730 --> 00:35:20,700
some days later, my grandson dies of poisoning.

526
00:35:20,700 --> 00:35:22,190
Rather suspicious.

527
00:35:22,210 --> 00:35:24,040
Why haven't you thrown me in a dungeon?

528
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:26,400
You spoke with Tyrion in this very brothel

529
00:35:26,400 --> 00:35:28,330
on the day that you arrived.

530
00:35:28,830 --> 00:35:30,120
What did you discuss?

531
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:32,030
You think we conspired together?

532
00:35:32,040 --> 00:35:33,390
What did you discuss?

533
00:35:33,390 --> 00:35:35,580
The death of my sister.

534
00:35:36,900 --> 00:35:38,640
For which you blame me.

535
00:35:38,640 --> 00:35:40,710
She was raped and murdered by the Mountain.

536
00:35:41,060 --> 00:35:43,610
The Mountain follows your orders.

537
00:35:43,610 --> 00:35:45,190
Of course I blame you.

538
00:35:45,190 --> 00:35:48,070
Here I stand unarmed, unguarded.

539
00:35:48,150 --> 00:35:49,440
Should I be concerned?

540
00:35:49,440 --> 00:35:50,950
You are unarmed and unguarded,

541
00:35:50,950 --> 00:35:53,200
because you know me better than that.

542
00:35:54,240 --> 00:35:55,800
I am a man of reason.

543
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:57,440
If I cut your throat today,

544
00:35:57,440 --> 00:35:59,450
I will be drawn and quartered tomorrow.

545
00:35:59,450 --> 00:36:01,420
Men at war commit all kinds of crimes

546
00:36:01,420 --> 00:36:02,940
without their superiors' knowledge.

547
00:36:02,940 --> 00:36:05,950
So you deny involvement in Elia's murder?

548
00:36:06,830 --> 00:36:08,470
Categorically.

549
00:36:17,620 --> 00:36:20,140
I would like to speak with the Mountain.

550
00:36:20,140 --> 00:36:22,660
I'm sure he would enjoy speaking with you.

551
00:36:22,660 --> 00:36:25,290
He might not enjoy it as much as he thinks he would.

552
00:36:27,480 --> 00:36:30,000
