557
00:36:41,920 --> 00:36:43,330
I will preside.

558
00:36:43,330 --> 00:36:46,250
Mace Tyrell will serve as the second judge.

559
00:36:47,110 --> 00:36:49,220
I would like you to be the third.

560
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:50,370
Why?

561
00:36:50,560 --> 00:36:54,180
Not long ago, the Tyrells sided with Renly Baratheon.

562
00:36:54,520 --> 00:36:57,230
Declared themselves enemies of the throne.

563
00:36:57,250 --> 00:36:59,480
Now they are our strongest allies.

564
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:01,820
Well, you made the Tyrell girl a queen.

565
00:37:02,080 --> 00:37:05,820
Asking me to judge at your son's trial isn't quite as tempting.

566
00:37:05,820 --> 00:37:08,910
I will also invite you to sit on the small council

567
00:37:09,120 --> 00:37:12,650
to serve as one of the new king's principal advisors.

568
00:37:18,670 --> 00:37:23,400
I never realized you had such respect for Dorne, Lord Tywin.

569
00:37:23,420 --> 00:37:27,460
We are not the Seven Kingdoms until Dorne returns to the fold.

570
00:37:27,460 --> 00:37:31,120
The king is dead. The Greyjoys are in open rebellion.

571
00:37:31,120 --> 00:37:33,870
A wildling army marches on the Wall.

572
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:38,260
And in the East, a Targaryen girl has three dragons.

573
00:37:40,600 --> 00:37:43,710
Before long, she will turn her eyes to Westeros.

574
00:37:44,040 --> 00:37:46,180
Only the Dornish managed to resist

575
00:37:46,180 --> 00:37:48,760
Aegon Targaryen and his dragons.

576
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:52,210
You're saying you need us?

577
00:37:53,650 --> 00:37:56,180
That must be hard for you to admit.

578
00:37:57,300 --> 00:37:58,730
We need each other.

579
00:38:00,180 --> 00:38:03,040
You help me serve justice to the king's assassins

580
00:38:03,040 --> 00:38:06,290
and I will help you serve justice to Elia's.

581
00:38:25,850 --> 00:38:26,930
Podrick.

582
00:38:28,600 --> 00:38:29,800
Apologies for the stench.

583
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:31,110
I brought you some wine, my lord,

584
00:38:31,110 --> 00:38:32,180
but they took it from me.

585
00:38:32,180 --> 00:38:33,480
A noble effort.

586
00:38:33,660 --> 00:38:35,860
They didn't find the candles, though.

587
00:38:36,970 --> 00:38:38,840
A quill, some parchment,

588
00:38:39,020 --> 00:38:41,680
duck sausage, almonds,

589
00:38:42,210 --> 00:38:44,090
and some hard cheese.

590
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:45,650
You're a good lad.

591
00:38:46,940 --> 00:38:48,430
Any word of Shae?

592
00:38:48,870 --> 00:38:50,620
I've heard nothing, my lord.

593
00:38:50,850 --> 00:38:52,760
I suppose that's a good thing.

594
00:38:54,210 --> 00:38:56,800
