This is farewell.

679
00:42:51,330 --> 00:42:52,360
Farewell, my lord.

680
00:42:58,400 --> 00:42:59,120
Pod.

681
00:43:03,740 --> 00:43:06,410
There has never lived a more loyal squire.

682
00:43:30,860 --> 00:43:32,340
Mother says it's time to eat.

683
00:43:32,350 --> 00:43:36,010
What's she got boiling? Wait. Wait. Let me guess.

684
00:43:36,210 --> 00:43:37,440
-Potatoes.  -Potatoes.

685
00:43:37,440 --> 00:43:41,460
Well, no one boils a potato better than your mom. She got.

686
00:43:44,040 --> 00:43:44,970
The wildlings!

687
00:43:45,140 --> 00:43:46,000
Guymon!

688
00:43:48,560 --> 00:43:49,320
Hide.

689
00:43:50,030 --> 00:43:50,800
Hide!

690
00:44:42,970 --> 00:44:46,100
-You know how to get to Castle Black?  -Yes. Yes.

691
00:44:54,540 --> 00:44:55,720
Those your parents?

692
00:44:57,880 --> 00:44:58,940
Open your eyes.

693
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:02,100
I'm going to eat them.

694
00:45:03,180 --> 00:45:04,110
Do you hear me?

695
00:45:04,740 --> 00:45:07,220
I'm going to eat your dead mama

696
00:45:07,420 --> 00:45:09,980
and I'm going to eat your dead papa.

697
00:45:11,180 --> 00:45:14,300
Go tell the crows at Castle Black.

698
00:45:23,100 --> 00:45:24,130
We need to teach them a lesson

699
00:45:24,130 --> 00:45:25,760
about the way we deal with their kind.

700
00:45:25,760 --> 00:45:26,650
-Aye!  -Aye!

701
00:45:26,870 --> 00:45:30,130
Three dozen bodies with slit throats tossed off the top of the Wall.

702
00:45:30,760 --> 00:45:33,070
-Seems like that would be a good lesson.  -Aye!

703
00:45:33,090 --> 00:45:35,790
If we go after them, we'll be giving them what they want.

704
00:45:36,560 --> 00:45:40,150
They want to draw us out, pick us off a few at a time.

705
00:45:40,310 --> 00:45:43,110
We have just over 100 men.

706
00:45:43,480 --> 00:45:46,990
And that's including stewards and builders.

707
00:45:47,200 --> 00:45:50,500
And me. We can't afford to lose a single man.

708
00:45:51,190 --> 00:45:54,410
We must remember our first responsibility.

709
00:45:55,340 --> 00:45:57,990
We are the watchers on the Wall.

710
00:45:59,170 --> 00:46:00,870
There's got to be a way to protect them.

711
00:46:02,450 --> 00:46:05,140
You're a champion of the common people, Lord Snow.

712
00:46:05,140 --> 00:46:07,810
What do you say to Brother Pyp's proposition?

713
00:46:12,600 --> 00:46:14,100
Mance Rayder is coming.

714
00:46:16,520 --> 00:46:18,300
If the wildlings breach the Wall,

715
00:46:18,700 --> 00:46:21,470
they'll roll over everything and everyone for 1,000 miles

716
00:46:21,470 --> 00:46:23,580
before they reach an army that can stop them.

717
00:46:27,110 --> 00:46:29,210
We need to shore up Castle Black

718
00:46:30,320 --> 00:46:32,110
and we need to defend the Wall.

719
00:46:33,580 --> 00:46:35,330
That is our job.

720
00:46:42,240 --> 00:46:43,390
Rangers returning.

721
00:46:50,820 --> 00:46:51,670
Help him.

722
00:46:54,090 --> 00:46:56,560
Thought you'd have blue eyes by now.

723
00:47:01,280 --> 00:47:02,260
What took you so long?

724
00:47:02,390 --> 00:47:04,530
-We were held up.  -By what?

725
00:47:05,180 --> 00:47:06,040
Chains.

726
00:47:06,190 --> 00:47:09,660
We were guests of the mutineers at Craster's Keep.

727
00:47:09,680 --> 00:47:11,880
-And the mutineers stayed?  -They're not going anywhere.

728
00:47:12,680 --> 00:47:14,840
They've got Craster's food and his wives.

729
00:47:15,640 --> 00:47:16,580
Poor girls.

730
00:47:16,720 --> 00:47:19,210
Never thought they'd miss their daddy.

731
00:47:19,420 --> 00:47:20,890
Karl's running things now.

732
00:47:21,080 --> 00:47:23,190
He's the one who put a knife through Craster's mouth.

733
00:47:23,490 --> 00:47:25,190
We need to ride north and kill them all.

734
00:47:25,190 --> 00:47:26,750
We just went over this, boy.

735
00:47:26,870 --> 00:47:29,050
-Justice can wait.  -It's not about justice.

736
00:47:31,630 --> 00:47:34,850
I told the wildlings we had over 1,000 men at Castle Black alone.

737
00:47:37,230 --> 00:47:39,480
Karl and the others know the truth as well as we do.

738
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:43,330
How long do you think they'll keep that information to themselves

739
00:47:43,330 --> 00:47:45,620
when the wildlings are peeling their fingernails off?

740
00:47:47,350 --> 00:47:50,220
Mance has all he needs to crush us, he just doesn't know it yet.

741
00:47:51,240 --> 00:47:53,420
As soon as he gets his hands on them, he will.

742
00:47:54,720 --> 00:47:56,740
Then he'll throw his full strength at us.

743
00:47:57,440 --> 00:47:59,980
And even if every one of us kills 100 wildlings,

744
00:48:00,280 --> 00:48:02,500
there's still not a thing we can do to stop them.

745
00:48:05,140 --> 00:48:07,080
I don't think I can kill 100 wildlings.

746
00:49:10,710 --> 00:49:11,740
Are they attacking?

747
00:49:13,180 --> 00:49:14,230
A single rider.

748
00:49:16,070 --> 00:49:17,520
A champion of Meereen.

749
00:49:18,720 --> 00:49:21,070
They want you to send your own champion against him.

750
00:49:47,650 --> 00:49:48,530
What is he doing?

751
00:49:49,790 --> 00:49:51,320
I believe he means to.

752
00:49:59,190 --> 00:50:02,780
He says that we're an army of men without man parts.

753
00:50:03,190 --> 00:50:05,840
He claims you are no woman at all, but a man who

754
00:50:06,830 --> 00:50:08,570
hides his cock in his own asshole.

755
00:50:09,460 --> 00:50:11,940
Ignore him, Your Grace. These are meaningless words.

756
00:50:12,180 --> 00:50:13,580
They're not meaningless if half the city

757
00:50:13,580 --> 00:50:15,510
